[list]
[*]Fixed: feeding a patient or a prisoner changed colonists out of uniform and back. The job starts wherever the meal is stored, so a doctor in scrubs changed out before fetching a meal from the freezer, then back into scrubs for the next tend, and a warden with a stand in the cell did the same. A meal run now leaves the uniform alone in both directions: whoever is wearing one keeps it on for the trip, and nobody is dressed for one. That covers feeding patients and sick animals, feeding prisoners and delivering their food, and Biotech's two hemogen jobs.
[*]A colonist whose stand is outside their allowed area is no longer sent to it. They used to be, and the trip was called off before they took a step, then tried again at the next job and every one after, so they never changed back. On the way in, a stand of their own outside the area also beat a shared stand inside it. Stands outside a colonist's allowed area are now passed over. Someone already wearing that stand's outfit keeps it on until the stand is back inside their area, and the stand's inspect pane says so. Change back still works, since it is an order. Better Pawn Control's alert mode can move every colonist's area at once, which is the easiest way to run into this.
[*]Common Sense: with its "haul ingredients over doing bills" setting on, which is how it ships, a cook in uniform changed out to fetch an ingredient from outside the kitchen, then changed back in for the bill. When the next job in line is the stand's own work in its room, an errand slotted in ahead of it is now done in uniform. Vanilla's own opportunistic hauling, which picks something up on the way to a bill, lines the jobs up the same way and gets the same treatment.
[*]Pick Up And Haul: a colonist who hauled out of their work room in uniform walked back to the stand with full pockets to change before unloading. The unload, and the extra haul that mod queues when it spots more nearby, now keep the uniform on, and their next ordinary job changes them back.
[*]The switch on a recreation or sleep stand read "Shift stand (no work here yet)" while the stand was working. It now names what the stand dresses for, as the inspect pane always did.
[*]With several stands selected, each one now shows its own switch and its own Set owner button. They used to merge into one button whose click opened a single stand's window, which left the other stands as they were while looking as if every one had been set.
[*]Change back's tooltip said colonists do not change back on their own while the map is under threat. They do, at their next job that leaves the room. The button is for when that is not soon enough.
[*]Ticking Fishing on a stand still does nothing, however the stand is set up. Fishing happens on open water, and dressing for it waits for stands that can serve more than their own room.
[/list]
